course: dictionary
lesson: 15402
title: Spontaneous: sudden and not planned
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Spontaneous» means sudden and not planned. If you decide to jump in a puddle just because you feel like it, that jump is spontaneous.
explain: «We had a spontaneous picnic in the park when the sun came out after lunch.» Nobody wrote it in a plan. The clue is that it started suddenly, so spontaneous fits.
explain: In a story, a spontaneous character is lively and free, and does things naturally. «The crowd gave spontaneous applause» means everyone clapped at once, without being asked to.
explain: Check by swapping in a meaning. If "unplanned" still makes sense in the sentence, you have it. Spontaneous is an adjective, and spontaneously is the adverb: «She laughed spontaneously.»
fact: Spontaneous means happening or done suddenly, without being planned.
fact: A spontaneous person does things on the spur of the moment, naturally and freely.
fact: «Spontaneous» can also be a science word: something that happens by itself, without being caused from outside.
fact: «Spontaneous combustion» means something catches fire by itself, with no spark from outside.
fact: «Spontaneous applause» means people clap suddenly, without being asked to.
exercise: «We had a spontaneous picnic when the sun came out.» What does spontaneous mean? | Old and broken | *Sudden and not planned | Cold and wet | Very large and expensive
exercise: Which phrase describes people clapping suddenly, without being asked? | Silent seats | *Spontaneous applause | Long speeches | Empty hall
exercise: Mia went to the beach that afternoon without telling anyone. Her trip was | Planned for weeks | *Spontaneous | Boring and slow | Sleepy
test: «The class made a spontaneous plan to sing for the head teacher.» What does spontaneous suggest? | Sad and quiet | Planned weeks ago | *Happening suddenly, not planned | Very old
test: What does spontaneous combustion mean? | A loud noise from a crowd | Something is washed and dried | *Something catches fire by itself, with no spark from outside | Food is cooked on a grill
exam: The adverb form of spontaneous is which word? | spontaneous | sponge | *spontaneously | spontaneity
